byebyetlsfix is senko's senkotlsfix (senko/senkotlsfix), taken without stl_proxy.c, which hooks connect
for senko's own socks port and is no use here.

changed on the way in: the paths (tlsfix_paths.h), the prefs plist and the log file, the default
bundle list (Troubadour instead of senko's app), and the gate stays off when a tlsfix package or
senko's copy sits in the substrate directory. the names carry bye so they never meet senko's.

the securetransport and trust hooks use substrate's MSHookFunction instead of fishhook.
on ios 9.3.6, shared-cache calls bypass the imported symbol pointers, leaving cfnetwork on
system tls 1.2 even with the shim loaded. the empty SecTrustSetAnchorCertificates hook is removed.
ssl contexts use the corefoundation finalizer for teardown on ios 5 and later, because
SSLDisposeContext is a desktop api. the finalizer lookup is guarded; without it the shim
leaves securetransport unchanged and logs the missing lifecycle hook.
